# Story 40: Inspecting Your Workspace (45s)
# Hook: Lost track of your layout? A handful of ## commands map your entire workspace.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-040-inspecting-your-workspace.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 9

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Lost track of your layout? A handful of ## commands map your entire workspace.

[00:03.0 --> 00:07.0]
Start rysh and build a small layout to inspect.

[00:07.0 --> 00:13.0]
Ctrl+P then n splits right, giving us a second pane in a new group.

[00:13.0 --> 00:18.0]
Double-Escape over to rysh mode so we can issue inspection commands.

[00:18.0 --> 00:24.0]
##pane info shows the active pane's details -- id, mode, given-name, and status.

[00:24.0 --> 00:30.0]
##tab list shows every tab with its pane count; ##lane list shows the columns in this tab.

[00:30.0 --> 00:36.0]
##pg list -- short for panegroup list -- enumerates every pane group in the active tab.

[00:36.0 --> 00:42.0]
And ##pg layout prints the full tab tree: lanes, groups, and stacked panes, all in one view.

[00:42.0 --> 00:45.0]
Five commands, and you can see your whole workspace at a glance.

